    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1022">

                <pb facs="1411" n="1399" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.92/12–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-17T17:00:00+00:00">December 17,
                            1945—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 17—3:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13208. ReDepts 10812, Dec 14; Embs 13197, Dec 17.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d1022-f1"
                    /> In view of fact that Dept’s 10783, December 13, 8 p.m., had not yet arrived,
                    we were unable to discuss detailed objections of Dept to British-Siamese
                    agreement with Foreign Office this afternoon. However we did obtain from
                    Wilson-Young, Acting Head of Far East Dept during absence Bennett in Moscow,
                    definite assurance that no agreement would be signed prior to Wednesday evening
                    Dec 19 London time. He said while it was not certain it would be signed the
                    following day he could give no assurances. Wilson-Young read US [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">us?</hi>] text of Foreign Office telegram sent to
                    British Embassy Washington Dec 14 dealing with rice collecting organization and
                    with strategic clauses of British-Siamese agreement. On question of clauses C–1
                    and C–2, British Embassy was authorized to give Dept written assurance along
                    lines outlined in this Embs 12848, Dec 7. In view of this Foreign Office
                    message, does Dept still desire signing of agreement held up beyond Wednesday
                    evening?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1022-f1" n="53" xml:id="d1022-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; the former quoted telegram 65, December 14, 11 a.m., from the
                    Political Adviser in Siam, <ref target="#pg1397">p. 1397</ref>, and the latter
                    reported receipt of telegram 10812 at 11:30 p.m., December 16.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
